# CarPlay Phone HOST project instructions

## Objective

Produce the platform-independent, event-driven C11-style PSEUDOCODE Phone HOST described in
`docs/wireless-phone-host/project-goal.md`. Work in `D:\ios-carplay` using existing
WSL Ubuntu-24.04. Other historical project directories are read-only.

User changed the goal to pseudocode. New primary artifacts belong in `pseudocode/`:
Include explanatory Chinese comments covering inputs, conditions, data ownership,
failure handling and evidence/OPEN boundaries, rather than bare function skeletons.
readable protocol/state/data handling with per-rule provenance and explicit OPEN
operations. Existing `reference/` executable C remains an experimental validation
baseline; do not expand runtime APIs merely to satisfy pseudocode delivery.
Syntax checks of pseudocode are not execution/interoperability evidence. Do not
invent wire values, private enums or accepting trust providers for completeness.

After each completed substage, report where the overall workflow has reached,
which parts remain, and the next/current active work. A scoped control predicate
completion must not be reported as completion of all Bluetooth/iAP2 or auth.

Prioritize the head unit's protocol interfaces, state transitions, and external /
internal data processing: Bluetooth/iAP2, Wi-Fi endpoint handoff, AirPlay security
and control, video/audio/microphone/input, then full lifecycle interoperability.
Use `reference/reports/project-status.json` and the latest per-rule evidence to
locate current progress. Complete the next prerequisite transaction before claiming
the dependent stage is ready.

## Evidence and implementation

- Cache queries: use `tools/ipsw-research/query-phone-decompiler.py` first.
  Run `python3 tools/ipsw-research/query-phone-decompiler.py index` after the
  initial cache and each added batch (refresh cache-union index first when
  necessary). Query by message ID/address and depth-one context; do not reread
  all C outputs for each message. Report actual query commands, addresses,
  raw/source hashes, evidence paths and unresolved items. Label graph edges
  as cached-assembly direct BL, external B tail call or unresolved indirect
  dispatch. Literal/name hits alone do not establish a protocol mapping.
- Latest workflow: batch-extract/decompile relevant firmware components and
  cache real C-style decompiler output with source/function addresses, original
  bytes and assembly links. Reuse the cache while reviewing message flows;
  avoid repeated isolated decompilation. Raw decompiler text is unreviewed
  research material, not annotated core code or independent protocol proof.
  Bind cache identity to source/tool/script/options hashes and record failures.
- User priority update: first inventory Phone HOST/head-unit wire messages by
  connection state, then verify direction, trigger, field encoding/parsing,
  response correlation and state changes. Prefer raw captures; only reverse
  engineer targeted firmware when captures cannot establish these behaviors.
  Defer system-internal work unrelated to peer messages. A complete inventory
  checklist does not mean the protocol or all listed candidates are confirmed.
  Clarification: captures are partial. Build the completeness inventory from
  current-firmware message registries/dispatchers and handlers, then validate
  wire bytes/order with captures. Do not restrict the inventory to observed IDs
  or postpone message-handler reverse engineering for uncaptured branches.
- Derive firmware-only rules independently from 24A446 original bytes/call context.
  Capture observations remain scoped to their own build/connection epoch and
  must not silently become current 24A446 rules. Freeze independent capture or
  firmware results before C changes and historical comparison.
  Reuse scoped confirmed addresses and tools, but do not infer rules from old C,
  old documentation, or a simulator. Snapshot existing artifacts, freeze new rules
  and original-instruction results, then compare old materials and implement C.
- Preserve earlier independent freezes and their tools. New research gets a new
  output directory; never rerun a writer against a frozen round.
- Distinguish static evidence, bounded original execution, versioned runtime
  observations, and local engineering policies / OPEN. Record binary hashes,
  addresses, raw bytes, inputs, substitutions, endpoint, and test scope.
- Restore protocol-essential semantics. OS Bluetooth/Wi-Fi/socket operations
  belong to adapters. Apple private queues, XPC layouts, and driver internals are
  research dependencies only when they affect peer-visible behavior or security.
- Never invent unknown protocol enums, security inputs, or provider contracts.
  Accepting verifier stubs are simulator-only and cannot close production trust.
- Preserve the old experimental profile. New local primitives do not enable the
  current profile. Reevaluate gates against complete required protocol contracts,
  without requiring every Apple private implementation detail.
- Separate restored, implemented, offline-tested, and live-verified status. No
  current capture or vehicle validation may be inferred from synthetic success.

## Verification

Use original-instruction boundary/counterexample comparisons where applicable,
independent capture/vector replay, meaningful module tests, full CTest, and
ASan/UBSan after integrated changes. Explain which operations were not executed.

From the project root in WSL:

```sh
python3 tools/ipsw-research/verify-reference.py
```

This writes `reference/reports/verification.json`. Follow current source hashes
and the per-round integrity reports. Explicitly list remaining protocol/material
gaps and real vehicle first-frame/audio/microphone/input/reconnect status.

## Model and context budget (user preference)

- Default delegated routine work (test execution, inventories, documentation and
  mechanical changes) to `gpt-6-luna` with `low` reasoning. Use `medium` only when
  routine work requires substantive code changes or diagnosis.
- Use `gpt-6.1-sol` with `medium` reasoning for independent ARM64/call-chain
  recovery and protocol/state-machine implementation. Escalate a specific hard
  ambiguity to `high`; do not default to xhigh/max/ultra or Astra.
- Start subagents with `fork_turns="none"`, a concise scoped brief, exact inputs,
  allowed output paths and a completion criterion. Do not copy the full chat.
- Prefer one active worker; use a second only for clearly independent work with
  nonoverlapping inputs/outputs that avoids duplicated research.
- Execute deterministic parsing, vector generation and testing with scripts.
  Return compact summaries and artifact paths instead of large dumps.
- Reuse existing frozen evidence and completed work. Do not rerun successful
  checks without source changes or a concrete unresolved concern. Keep required
  final verification, evidence boundaries and security checks intact.
- On a model usage-limit error, record partial outputs and stop retrying that
  model. A different model is not assumed to bypass an account-wide limit.
- These defaults govern agent-controlled delegations. Do not claim the current
  chat's model was changed without a supported setting change and confirmation.
